  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Nigeria Food_Hives Nourishing Cities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Description for CO Nigeria
Oxfam in Nigeria recognizes that promoting transparency and accountability through social and political participation of citizens is fundamental to effectively changing Nigeria#s narrative as a rich nation of poor people. Women constitute the majority of the poor, excluded from processes and decisions that affect their lives. The OCS therefore prioritizes policy influencing and citizen empowerment, especially for the most vulnerable to have a say in issues that affect their lives. This is the most effective strategy to unlock the potentials in Nigeria#s extractives sector to translate to resources for improved livingstandards. Oxfam puts women at the heart of our programmes to redress years of injustice and marginalization, enabling them live above violence realize their full potential, and contribute to nation building.

 Oxfam has been working through partners# both nationally and regionally in the area of public finance accountability in Nigeria, utilizing the one programme approach to create linkageswithin the various strands of these interventions. These include. Fair taxation campaign, enhancing transparency in payments in theextractives sector within the NEITI framework and promoting accountability through active citizen participation in the budget of states and the Federal government.  To give additional effect to this, Oxfam had since 2012 been working with Civil Society organizations and coalitions on the NEITI framework to increase the availability of fiscal information to citizens through the regular production of NEITI Audit Reports, and follow up with Remediation of findings. In effect, following the money. As a result of the support of Oxfam and the work of the partner CISLAC working on the NEITI project, there has been increased collaboration between the NEITI Secretariat and Civil Society. This resulted in Nigeria being recognized as the best implementing EITI country in Sidney Australia in 2014.</narrative>
  </description>
